## v2.6.0 (2026-08-06)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus issue #2382 / PR #2664 automation-loop review and merge path.
**Verification:** verified-ci.

### What changed
- Added the workflow-discovery trigger for suppressed directory errors and `--allow-empty` false-success risks.
- Recorded the `Path.iterdir()` correction and regression requirement.
- Recorded PR #2664’s exact-head NOGO-to-GO label transition, required-check completion, and conditional merge.

### Why
PR #2664 showed that a review can catch a real tool-error classification gap after the implementation head exists: `Path.glob()` suppressed an unreadable-directory `OSError`, so `--allow-empty` could incorrectly pass. The same-head implementation reply supplied the `Path.iterdir()` fix and regression evidence; only the subsequent exact-head review and loop-owned GO label authorized merge.

