## v2.2.0 (2026-08-04)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus issue #2633 / PR #2636 automation-loop review and merge path.
**Verification:** verified-ci.

### What changed

- Added the closed immutable GitHub worker request/receipt boundary for reply delivery, PR-review reconciliation, and merge-wait admission.
- Added per-job client ownership, same-repository serialization, receipt-before-state advancement, and operation-owned retry guidance.
- Defined merge-attempt accounting at conditional-request issuance and recorded PR #2636’s six-thread remediation, exact-head GO, required checks, and merge.

### Why

Issue #2633 showed that preserving exact-head authorization is not enough when stage steps synchronously perform retrying GitHub I/O: the review and merge path exceeded its responsiveness contract. A generic callable worker would have hidden mutable cross-thread coupling and shared-client ownership. PR #2636 instead used closed frozen requests, request-bearing immutable receipts, fresh job-scoped clients, and same-repository serialization. Readiness failures before a conditional merge spend no attempt; every post-request outcome does and is reconciled before retry. The final review matched `79974e422321f2ce0f840764f7a09bd6ca2f585b`, all six threads resolved, required checks passed, and conditional merge `d993cc1bfc6334ba9ced45452c4f98f08303b453` completed.

