## v1.6.0 (2026-07-28)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus issue #2507 / PR #2508 detached-review publication correction.
**Verification:** verified-ci.

### What changed

- Distinguished a clean detached review at the reviewed head from a clean detached review containing an agent-precommitted fix.
- Defined `expected_remote_sha` as a publication lease, not a disposable direct-scope reservation, when `publish_detached_head=True`.
- Added the current-head re-review, `state:implementation-go`, and conditional-merge sequence observed on corrected head `55300bb4`.

### Why

Worktree cleanliness cannot prove that an address agent made no change: the agent may have
committed the fix itself. Conversely, when the detached review remains exactly at the reviewed
remote head, direct-scope cleanup must not run because the branch belongs to the adopted open PR.
PR #2508 verified both states in regression tests and then completed the exact-head review and
merge path with all required checks green.

